mod:header_store_target;
// 2026-11-15 (landing 177d2b7, row 1: DEF-660's K-a2 as V1 with F6). A STORE INTO A STRING'S, CSTRING'S OR BUFFER'S STORAGE IS RECORDED BY WHERE THE HEADER
// LIVES. A callee `mk` stores a pointer through a header's `.ptr` crossed to `wild`, or through the header's own address (`(@b) =>! wild int64->->`). A header
// this frame owns (a local, or a by-value `move` parameter) holds the stored refs on its own chain, so a growth of the stored pointer's source, or a store of a
// view that dies with `mk`, is refused where the header holds it. A header the CALLER owns, reached through a pointer parameter (`p.h`, `self.h`, `p.i.h`,
// `p.hs[0i64]`), is the caller's storage: the store is the callee's summary's and is judged by BORROW-002 at the store, and the pointer parameter's own chain
// takes nothing (DEF-675's record, narrowed by this row: `lib/ntensor.npk`'s `set` stores through `self.cells.ptr`, and the record put `v` on `self`'s chain).
// Each face and each twin is refused by main (78f9b3a) too; its sites say which records the store makes. One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's.
// THE FACES: `nw_` a local (L) or by-value (P) buffer, string or cstring header's `.ptr`, or a buffer's address (a), stored on the named root (n), through a
// pointer local (q) or by a storing callee (c), the header then returned (r), stored through a parameter (p), pushed to the caller's `List` (l), or read back
// by `mk` after its `List` grew (g); `np_fxqg`, `np_mxqg`, `np_nxqg`, `np_axqg` the caller's header through a pointer parameter, in a field, `self`'s field,
// a field of a field and an array slot, the address spelling through a pointer local, read back after the growth.
// THE PRICES, two right programs this row refuses, each a cell of this file under a PRICE comment naming its twin: a header's `.ptr` held by a pointer local
// that is never read again, across the header's move into the caller's `List` or through a parameter (`nw_bLlq_ok`, `nw_bLpq_ok`). They are at parity with
// main's own refusals, the four cells after them: `b13_hdr_l_tw`, the header's address held (BORROW-013), and `b13_elem_l_tw`, `b13_elem_p_tw`, `b13_sl_l_tw`,
// a `List` element's address or a slice of it held across the `List`'s move (BORROW-015).
// The right controls are in `header_store_target_ok.npk`.
error:E5;
// nw_aLgq: see tools/mknw.py
func:mk_nw_aLgq = int64(int64->:g) {
    List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(2i64);
    drop list_push(@l, 7i64);
    buffer:b = buffer_new(16i64);
    wild int64->->:q = ((@b) =>! wild int64->->);
    <-q = (@l[0i64]) =>! wild int64->;
    loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@l, 1i64); }
    int64->:p = (<-((@b) =>! wild int64->->)) =>! int64->;
    pass <-p;
};
func:cell_main_nw_aLgq = int32() never fails {
    int64:k = 7i64;
    pass ((mk_nw_aLgq(@k) ?! E5) + 60i64) =>! int32;
};
